Summary
Today I worked on deploying my full-stack project, including both the frontend and backend. I used Vercel for hosting the frontend and Render for deploying the backend services. During the process, I configured the project deployment settings and connected the frontend with the backend API. I also faced an issue where the deployed application was showing a blank white screen, which I began troubleshooting by checking browser console errors. The error indicated a network-related issue affecting resource loading during deployment.
Outcomes
As a result of today’s work, the project is successfully deployed on both frontend and backend platforms, even though it is not yet fully functioning as expected. I identified that the main issue is related to a loading failure error (`ERR_HTTP2_PROTOCOL_ERROR`), which will require further debugging. I also gained a clearer understanding of how deployment configuration affects React application behavior in production. Additionally, I learned how frontend-backend integration issues can directly impact application rendering. Tomorrow’s focus will be on resolving the deployment error and ensuring the application loads correctly in the live environment.
  
